  "id": "Compound::DB00334 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Olanzapine is shown to bind to Cyp2c19, a cytochrome P450 enzyme, which is involved in the metabolism of various substrates. This binding is consistent across multiple paths, with all three paths indicating that Cyp2c19 participates in the activity of limonene monooxygenase, a key enzyme in the oxidation of limonene. The shared involvement of Cyp2c19 in the same metabolic pathway suggests a mechanistic link between Olanzapine and Cyp2c9, as all three paths indicate that Cyp2c19 is participated in by Cyp2c9. The high scores from the paths suggest a strong and consistent relationship, though the exact mechanism of how Olanzapine influences Cyp2c9 remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a direct interaction between Olanzapine and Cyp2c9 through the enzyme Cyp2c19, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise role of Cyp2c9 in this process.",
